    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear strategy: exploit favorable pitching matchups to bolster our efficiency, even as we remain hyper-vigilant regarding stolen base opportunities. **Kyle Tucker** (72.68) and **Heliot Ramos** (69.03) anchor the outfield as our premier plays. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a strong efficiency boost against the pitching profile of Wandy Peralta, while **Heliot Ramos** finds himself in an enviable position facing Sullivan, who carries a brutal 6.43 xERA. **Andy Pages** (68.87) is another critical start; while he faces the same pitcher as **Kyle Tucker**, the model identified a specific edge in the opponent's slow delivery, creating a high-upside environment for **Andy Pages** to pad our scarcest category, stolen bases. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start at 63.22, providing consistent elite-tier output despite a tougher matchup against Greene.\n\nRegarding roster management, the most difficult decision was keeping **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.28) on the bench. While his pedigree is unquestionable, the metrics favored **Josh Jung** (53.78) and the high-floor efficiency of our active infielders. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** fell victim to a combination of a challenging matchup against Gilbert and a negative park factor adjustment that widened the gap between his projected output and our starters. We are also monitoring the lineup status for **Jackson Merrill** (53.32); while he is currently penciled into the six-hole, his efficiency score is weighted by a significant stolen base opportunity, though he faces the stiffest test of the day against Yamamoto. Owners should note that while **Drake Baldwin**, **Liam Hicks**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Josh Lowe** all hold viable scores, their upside is tempered by the varying quality of their opposing starters. We will rely on the speed-weighted projections of **Andy Pages** and **Heliot Ramos** to carry the day as we navigate these matchups.",
